H.264: default profile-level-id to Baseline 3.0 instead of Level 1.0
====================================================================

When a remote's SDP offers H.264 with no profile-level-id in the fmtp line,
pjmedia falls back to the RFC 6184 default "42000A" — Baseline **Level 1.0**,
whose maximum frame size is QCIF (176x144). Nothing constrains the remote to
actually send QCIF, and a source that omits the attribute while sending CIF or
VGA produces a stream the Level 1.0 profile cannot represent. Every frame is
then discarded before it reaches the decoder and no video is ever rendered,
while audio and RTP statistics look perfectly healthy.

Observed on a TD1070 door panel: Asterisk offers `a=rtpmap:99 H264/90000` with
no fmtp, pjsip answers `profile-level-id=42000a`, and the incoming 640x480
stream renders nothing. When Asterisk happens to follow up with a re-INVITE
carrying `profile-level-id=42E01F`, the same stream decodes normally — so the
negotiated level, not the stream, is what gates decoding.

This raises the fallback to "42E01E" (Baseline, constraint_set0+1+2, Level 3.0
— up to 720x576), matching what the working re-INVITE negotiated. It only
changes behaviour where the peer supplied no profile-level-id at all; an
explicit attribute from the remote still wins.

Apply from the pjproject root with `git apply <patch>`, or via
build-pjsip-android.sh which applies it automatically post-clone.
---
diff --git a/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/vid_codec_util.c b/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/vid_codec_util.c
index 947a96f..171d772 100644
--- a/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/vid_codec_util.c
+++ b/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/vid_codec_util.c
@@ -465,9 +465,13 @@ PJ_DEF(pj_status_t) pjmedia_vid_codec_h264_parse_fmtp(
         }
     }
 
-    /* When profile-level-id is not specified, use default value "42000A" */
+    /* When profile-level-id is not specified, default to Baseline Level 3.0
+     * ("42E01E") rather than the spec's "42000A" (Level 1.0, QCIF 176x144).
+     * A remote that omits profile-level-id can still send CIF/VGA, which a
+     * Level 1.0 profile cannot represent, and every frame is then discarded.
+     */
     if (h264_fmtp->profile_idc == 0) {
-        const pj_str_t DEF_PROFILE = {"42000A", 6};
+        const pj_str_t DEF_PROFILE = {"42E01E", 6};
 
         status = init_h264_profile(&DEF_PROFILE, h264_fmtp);
         if (status != PJ_SUCCESS)
